  "text": "מוקד opposite the vertex $A$ is the midpoint of $BC$. Similarly, the midpoint of $AC$ is the midpoint opposite $B$, and the midpoint of $AB$ is the midpoint opposite $C$. Now consider the circles with diameters $AP$, $BQ$, and $CR$. These three circles intersect at points $X$, $Y$, and $Z$, respectively, where each point of intersection is the intersection of the two circles.\n\nTo determine the area of $\\triangle XYZ$, we need to find the coordinates of $X$, $Y$, and $Z$ and calculate the area of the triangle formed by these points. For simplicity, we can use coordinate geometry. Assume $A$ is at $(0,0)$, $B$ is at $(13,0)$, and $C$ is at $(x,y)$. The midpoint of $BC$ is at $\\left(\\frac{13+x}{2}, \\frac{y}{2}\\right)$, and the midpoint of $AC$ is at $\\left(\\frac{x}{2}, \\frac{\\sqrt{x^2 - 169}}{2}\\right)$. \n\nHowever, calculating the exact coordinates of $X$, $Y$, and $Z$ directly can be complex. We can simplify the problem by noting that the points of intersection of the circles (specifically, the second intersection points with the other circles) have coordinates that follow a simple pattern due to the symmetry and properties of the triangle.\n\nGiven that the sides of the triangle are $AB = 13$, $BC = 14$, and $CA = 15$, we can use the fact that the locus of the intersection points of the circles with diameters opposite the vertices is a triangle similar to the original triangle and scaled down. The ratio of the sides of $\\triangle XYZ$ to the sides of $\\triangle ABC$ is $\\sqrt{\\frac{a+b+c}{3}}$, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are the lengths of the sides of $\\triangle ABC$. \n\nTherefore, the ratio of the sides of $\\triangle XYZ$ to $\\triangle ABC$ is $\\sqrt{\\frac{13+14+15}{3}} = \\sqrt{22}$. This means that the area of $\\triangle XYZ$ is $\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{22}{3}}\\right)^2 = \\frac{22}{3}$ times the area of $\\triangle ABC$.\n\nThe area of $\\triangle ABC$ can be found using Heron's formula:\n\n\\[\ns = \\frac{13+14+15}{2} = 21\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\sqrt{21(21-13)(21-14)(21-15)} = \\sqrt{21 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6} = \\sqrt{7056} = 84\n\\]\n\nSo the area of $\\triangle XYZ$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area of } \\triangle XYZ = \\frac{22}{3} \\times 84 = 66 \\times 2 = 132\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of $\\triangle XYZ$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{5}}\n\\]\n\nERRQ (Error Result Queue) is a mechanism for diagnosing and sharing error information with the rest of the application recognition centers once an error is encountered. At the same time, to check the results of notifications, it can also dynamically pull notifications from other recognized devices around.\nA. Correct\nB. Incorrect\nAnswer:\nA\n\nThe birthmark of modern nursing begins with:\nA. Florence Nightingale's 'Lady with the Lamp'\nB. The English nurse Florence Nightingale\nC. Sir Thomas Grey\nD. Onsley\nAnswer:\nA\n\nAccording to GB50208-2011 'Code for acceptance of waterproofing works on underground projects', which test must be conducted on the waterproofing materials of underground projects?\nA. Insulation pressure strength test B. Water absorption rate test C. Seepage resistance test D. Impermeability test\nAnswer:\nC",
